1
00:00:07,716 --> 00:00:10,552
One minute to go.

2
00:00:10,635 --> 00:00:14,389
Well then, Ms. Utahime Iori,

3
00:00:14,472 --> 00:00:17,892
please give us a touching
and encouraging speech.

4
00:00:17,976 --> 00:00:18,810
What?

5
00:00:18,893 --> 00:00:21,563
Well…

6
00:00:21,646 --> 00:00:23,189
Well…

7
00:00:23,273 --> 00:00:26,401
Although injuries are inevitable…

8
00:00:26,484 --> 00:00:28,737
Well…

9
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:30,613
Just help each other from time to time.

10
00:00:30,697 --> 00:00:32,073
Something like that?

11
00:00:32,157 --> 00:00:33,575
Time's up.

12
00:00:33,658 --> 00:00:36,578
Gojo, you…

13
00:00:36,661 --> 00:00:39,956
With that,
the Sister-School Goodwill Event…

14
00:00:40,498 --> 00:00:43,626
begins!

15
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:45,545
Show some respect to your seniors!

16
00:00:46,212 --> 00:00:47,172
Was that Ichiro?

17
00:00:47,255 --> 00:00:48,715
Idiot.

18
00:00:49,382 --> 00:00:50,884
Where's Todo?

19
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:53,762
Why do you assume I would know?

20
00:00:53,845 --> 00:00:55,472
Let's get along well.

21
00:01:04,898 --> 00:01:06,983
Where could the Cursed Spirits' boss be?

22
00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:10,570
I think it will be placed
in the middle of both teams.

23
00:01:10,653 --> 00:01:12,822
But it probably won't stay still.

24
00:01:13,406 --> 00:01:16,076
When the time comes,
divide into Panda team and Megumi team

25
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:17,994
since they are good at finding enemies.

26
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:20,997
We'll leave the rest to you, Yuji.

27
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:22,373
Got it!

28
00:01:26,669 --> 00:01:29,798
Where are you going?

29
00:01:31,299 --> 00:01:32,383
That's a small fry.

30
00:01:37,013 --> 00:01:38,640
Stop, Maki!

31
00:01:46,397 --> 00:01:49,818
All right! Seems like everyone's here.

32
00:01:49,901 --> 00:01:52,320
Come at me together!

33
00:01:57,033 --> 00:01:58,201
Split up!

34
00:02:01,913 --> 00:02:03,623
Todo's alone.

35
00:02:04,249 --> 00:02:06,584
It was the right choice to change to Yuji.

36
00:02:11,089 --> 00:02:13,508
I already knew this, but he's a monster.

37
00:02:13,591 --> 00:02:16,010
Yes. So ignore them.

38
00:03:58,738 --> 00:04:00,949
BEFORE THE TEAM BATTLE

39
00:04:01,032 --> 00:04:04,994
Todo will definitely rush to defeat us.

40
00:04:05,078 --> 00:04:08,831
Mai might also follow him
to come after me.

41
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:12,543
Todo is a monster.

42
00:04:12,627 --> 00:04:17,715
In the worst-case scenario,
everyone will be wiped out.

43
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:25,431
Originally, I planned to leave Panda
or Megumi to hold him. But now…

44
00:04:26,849 --> 00:04:29,519
Itadori, this task will be yours.

45
00:04:29,602 --> 00:04:30,478
What?

46
00:04:31,312 --> 00:04:34,232
I don't want to remove people
who can find the enemy.

47
00:04:35,108 --> 00:04:39,320
You don't have to beat him.
Just hold him back for a while.

48
00:04:39,404 --> 00:04:41,406
But you need to be bold.

49
00:04:41,489 --> 00:04:44,200
To put it bluntly, you're unexpected help,

50
00:04:44,284 --> 00:04:46,411
so it won't affect us
if you have to retire.

51
00:04:46,494 --> 00:04:47,662
That's too much!

52
00:04:48,413 --> 00:04:50,123
I'm sorry, Megumi.

53
00:04:50,206 --> 00:04:52,542
You wanted to fight Todo, didn't you?

54
00:04:53,376 --> 00:04:55,420
No, I don't mind it.

55
00:04:55,503 --> 00:04:57,005
You're so calm.

56
00:04:58,798 --> 00:05:01,384
But, Panda, since I'm fighting him…

57
00:05:01,467 --> 00:05:02,635
-What?
-What?

58
00:05:03,511 --> 00:05:05,471
I'll win.

59
00:05:09,434 --> 00:05:11,144
Your speed is quite good.

60
00:05:11,728 --> 00:05:14,689
Are you serious?
I hit pretty hard just now.

61
00:05:21,654 --> 00:05:23,239
Payback time, first-year student.

62
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:24,907
Try your best to defend!

63
00:05:42,759 --> 00:05:44,343
My hand's still intact, right?

64
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:47,680
I thought it flew off.

65
00:05:47,764 --> 00:05:51,434
If the Cursed Spirit wasn't there,
I would've been in big trouble.

66
00:06:24,425 --> 00:06:25,802
Over already?

67
00:06:33,184 --> 00:06:35,853
All right. Who's next?

68
00:06:41,859 --> 00:06:43,611
Are you serious?

69
00:06:51,035 --> 00:06:54,872
You keep punching my head.

70
00:06:54,956 --> 00:06:57,792
What if I become dumber?

71
00:06:58,751 --> 00:07:00,378
Don't worry.

72
00:07:00,461 --> 00:07:05,383
Takada said,
"It's better for a boy to be stupid."

73
00:07:05,466 --> 00:07:07,051
Who's that?

74
00:07:07,135 --> 00:07:09,387
I'm not interested in idols.

75
00:07:09,470 --> 00:07:12,056
Then why do you know she's an idol?

76
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:14,100
You know her, don't you?

77
00:07:14,725 --> 00:07:17,145
What's your name, first-year?

78
00:07:17,228 --> 00:07:18,646
Yuji Itadori.

79
00:07:18,729 --> 00:07:21,107
I see. Yuji Itadori.

80
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:23,651
I have a question for you.

81
00:07:25,445 --> 00:07:27,655
What type of woman do you like?

82
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:29,740
What?

83
00:07:30,241 --> 00:07:32,160
What type of woman?

84
00:07:32,243 --> 00:07:34,662
Why are you asking this now?

85
00:07:34,745 --> 00:07:38,166
Don't mind me.
It's just my way of evaluating people.

86
00:07:40,626 --> 00:07:44,672
I don't understand,
but if I had to choose…

87
00:07:48,426 --> 00:07:52,763
A girl with big head
and big butt, perhaps?

88
00:07:52,847 --> 00:07:55,099
Someone like Jennifer Lawrence.

89
00:07:57,727 --> 00:07:59,645
What?

90
00:08:05,902 --> 00:08:09,822
SHOUNEN WEEKLY MAGAZINE

91
00:08:10,531 --> 00:08:12,909
The new series is quite interesting.

92
00:08:12,992 --> 00:08:13,826
Really?

93
00:08:16,537 --> 00:08:17,663
-What?
-What?

94
00:08:30,635 --> 00:08:32,553
I'm going to confess to Takada.

95
00:08:33,137 --> 00:08:34,889
What? Don't do that!

96
00:08:34,972 --> 00:08:38,267
I don't want to comfort you.
It's troublesome.

97
00:08:38,351 --> 00:08:40,978
Why are you sure that I would get dumped?

98
00:08:43,481 --> 00:08:46,984
On the other hand,
why do you think she would agree?

99
00:08:47,068 --> 00:08:50,696
Anne Sullivan once said this
to Helen Keller.

100
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:55,201
"How can a fool think about losing
before he does it?"

101
00:08:55,284 --> 00:08:57,036
That's what Inoki said.

102
00:08:58,538 --> 00:09:00,206
I'm sorry.

103
00:09:00,289 --> 00:09:02,500
I already have someone I like.

104
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:23,145
Is it possible
that I'm that someone she likes?

105
00:09:23,729 --> 00:09:25,439
How could it be possible?

106
00:09:28,609 --> 00:09:30,403
Come on. Let's go.

107
00:09:32,863 --> 00:09:34,949
I'll buy you ramen.

108
00:09:50,881 --> 00:09:54,343
"At home, we are invincible…"

109
00:09:56,345 --> 00:10:00,766
Looks like we're best friends.

110
00:10:00,850 --> 00:10:02,852
Even though you just asked for my name?

111
00:10:04,645 --> 00:10:06,689
Just go straight.

112
00:10:06,772 --> 00:10:08,274
But Todo is there.

113
00:10:08,357 --> 00:10:12,236
It's okay. He's the one who said
we can do as we please.

114
00:10:20,494 --> 00:10:22,955
New Shadow Style, Simple Domain!

115
00:10:25,416 --> 00:10:26,417
Batto Sword Drawing!

116
00:10:31,839 --> 00:10:33,507
His response is quick!

117
00:10:33,591 --> 00:10:35,092
Although I hesitated,

118
00:10:35,176 --> 00:10:37,511
my attack didn't scratch him at all!

119
00:10:43,142 --> 00:10:44,810
I'm surrounded.

120
00:10:45,519 --> 00:10:48,814
What? These guys…

121
00:10:48,898 --> 00:10:50,316
Aren't they…

122
00:10:54,111 --> 00:10:55,780
trying to kill me?

123
00:11:01,452 --> 00:11:02,703
This technique…

124
00:11:02,787 --> 00:11:03,704
What?

125
00:11:03,788 --> 00:11:06,207
I swapped positions with Itadori!

126
00:11:07,875 --> 00:11:08,876
Hey.

127
00:11:10,169 --> 00:11:12,129
I told you, didn't I?

128
00:11:12,213 --> 00:11:14,465
I'll kill you if you get in my way.

129
00:11:15,091 --> 00:11:16,550
No.

130
00:11:16,634 --> 00:11:19,470
You said, "I'll kill you if you order me."

131
00:11:19,553 --> 00:11:21,347
Was that Itadori?

132
00:11:21,430 --> 00:11:24,600
No, was that Todo's cursed technique?

133
00:11:24,683 --> 00:11:27,311
It's all the same. Leave!

134
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:36,070
Retreating?

135
00:11:36,153 --> 00:11:37,154
Lame.

136
00:11:37,655 --> 00:11:39,115
I'm so glad!

137
00:11:39,615 --> 00:11:41,909
You must kill him.

138
00:11:41,992 --> 00:11:44,578
That depends on Itadori.

139
00:11:44,662 --> 00:11:46,414
Don't order me around.

140
00:11:46,497 --> 00:11:48,290
What's wrong with these guys?

141
00:11:48,374 --> 00:11:50,918
They want to kill me,
yet they're infighting.

142
00:11:52,711 --> 00:11:55,840
After all,
I'm not the kind of tasteless man

143
00:11:55,923 --> 00:11:58,134
who shows mercy to his best friend!

144
00:12:04,515 --> 00:12:05,641
Oh, man.

145
00:12:06,225 --> 00:12:08,394
That's why I said stay out of it.

146
00:12:09,061 --> 00:12:10,813
What a bad start.

147
00:12:11,647 --> 00:12:13,983
Since I'm in charge
of hunting Cursed Spirits,

148
00:12:14,066 --> 00:12:16,152
I need to find them from the air first.

149
00:12:18,279 --> 00:12:20,698
This is so troublesome.

150
00:12:21,282 --> 00:12:24,076
I'm going to work hard.
I'm cute today, as usual.

151
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:25,369
Knock her down.

152
00:12:27,455 --> 00:12:28,789
Oh, no!

153
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:33,544
Mai and Mechamaru, go help Nishimiya.

154
00:12:33,627 --> 00:12:37,214
-Understood.
-Okay, we need her anyway.

155
00:12:49,018 --> 00:12:50,186
Kamo.

156
00:12:50,895 --> 00:12:54,482
Are you guys planning to kill Itadori?

157
00:13:12,615 --> 00:13:13,532
Something is wrong.

158
00:13:13,616 --> 00:13:15,284
Something is weird.

159
00:13:15,367 --> 00:13:18,037
Kyoto team is moving as a whole.

160
00:13:18,704 --> 00:13:21,207
They are around the area
we separated from Yuji.

161
00:13:21,290 --> 00:13:23,626
Isn't everyone from Kyoto team there?

162
00:13:24,627 --> 00:13:26,962
Is the target there?

163
00:13:27,463 --> 00:13:28,422
No.

164
00:13:28,506 --> 00:13:30,799
Unless the Grade 2 Cursed Spirit
is cunning,

165
00:13:30,883 --> 00:13:32,510
the Divine Dog will detect it.

166
00:13:34,303 --> 00:13:38,307
Are they trying to kill Itadori?

167
00:13:38,390 --> 00:13:40,809
What's this? This is absurd.

168
00:13:45,231 --> 00:13:46,815
It's possible.

169
00:13:47,399 --> 00:13:48,317
Kelp.

170
00:13:48,901 --> 00:13:52,321
It's that I didn't feel hostility
from them,

171
00:13:52,905 --> 00:13:56,325
but that was before Yuji's
survival surprise.

172
00:13:58,369 --> 00:14:02,331
It's possible if that was
Principal Gakuganji's instruction.

173
00:14:02,414 --> 00:14:08,337
Is Kyoto team a group of cowards
who will obey orders to kill people?

174
00:14:08,420 --> 00:14:10,631
Our perceptions are different.

175
00:14:10,714 --> 00:14:14,343
You lived with Yuji before.

176
00:14:14,426 --> 00:14:18,055
We only just knew that he's a good guy.

177
00:14:18,138 --> 00:14:20,975
He's cheerful,
and that's rare among Jujutsu Sorcerers.

178
00:14:21,058 --> 00:14:22,351
However,

179
00:14:23,143 --> 00:14:25,854
for those who don't know Yuji,

180
00:14:25,938 --> 00:14:30,359
Sukuna's vessel is a scary existence.

181
00:14:31,110 --> 00:14:34,738
It's similar to exorcising curses.

182
00:14:35,281 --> 00:14:40,369
It's easy for Jujutsu Sorcerers
to cross the line in the first place.

183
00:14:43,956 --> 00:14:45,708
Megumi, let's go back.

184
00:14:46,458 --> 00:14:47,668
I'm sorry.

185
00:14:47,751 --> 00:14:49,795
What are you apologizing for?

186
00:14:50,379 --> 00:14:52,339
If our comrade dies,

187
00:14:52,423 --> 00:14:54,842
what's the point
of winning the Goodwill Event?

188
00:14:56,343 --> 00:15:00,472
Nobara and I will go confirm
Yuji's safety.

189
00:15:01,056 --> 00:15:02,766
He's not answering his phone.

190
00:15:02,850 --> 00:15:06,270
Toge will carry on to hunt Cursed Spirits.

191
00:15:06,854 --> 00:15:07,938
Bonito flakes.

192
00:15:08,022 --> 00:15:10,900
I know you're worried about Yuji too.

193
00:15:11,483 --> 00:15:14,153
But if my guess is right,

194
00:15:14,236 --> 00:15:20,409
they're trying to assassinate Yuji
in the chaos of team battle.

195
00:15:20,492 --> 00:15:24,079
There won't be any assassination
if the team battle ends.

196
00:15:24,163 --> 00:15:25,456
I see.

197
00:15:25,539 --> 00:15:26,415
Salmon.

198
00:15:26,498 --> 00:15:28,083
I'm worried about Maki, too.

199
00:15:28,584 --> 00:15:32,046
We can't let them kill Yuji,
and we'll win the team battle.

200
00:15:32,546 --> 00:15:33,923
Of course.

201
00:15:38,427 --> 00:15:41,013
Answer the call once it rings, Fushiguro!

202
00:15:42,014 --> 00:15:46,894
Speaking of which, why didn't the school
provide a radio or Bluetooth headset?

203
00:15:47,478 --> 00:15:49,104
I don't want it.

204
00:15:49,188 --> 00:15:51,941
It's distracting
and I'll be shocked when it rings.

205
00:15:52,024 --> 00:15:54,401
Just take it off during the battle!

206
00:15:59,365 --> 00:16:00,824
That hurt.

207
00:16:02,952 --> 00:16:05,537
So that's Fushiguro's Nue…

208
00:16:06,038 --> 00:16:07,873
The wings are electrified.

209
00:16:07,957 --> 00:16:10,834
It will affect my movements temporarily.

210
00:16:13,212 --> 00:16:18,008
-Nishimiya!
-Nishimiya!

211
00:16:18,592 --> 00:16:21,512
-Let's play.
-Let's play.

212
00:16:21,595 --> 00:16:24,765
So uncultivated and not cute.

213
00:16:25,432 --> 00:16:29,228
Kamo, are you guys trying to kill Itadori?

214
00:16:29,812 --> 00:16:33,232
What if I say yes?

215
00:16:33,315 --> 00:16:35,317
You failed.

216
00:16:35,401 --> 00:16:38,737
Itadori won't be killed so easily.

217
00:16:43,158 --> 00:16:44,660
We have no reason to kill him.

218
00:16:45,411 --> 00:16:46,578
There is a reason.

219
00:16:46,662 --> 00:16:49,456
At least, the higher-ups
and the Big Three Sorcerer Family do.

220
00:17:21,697 --> 00:17:23,741
What great endurance.

221
00:17:23,824 --> 00:17:26,493
He also takes advantage
of the terrain actively!

222
00:17:28,162 --> 00:17:29,621
He's gone.

223
00:17:32,708 --> 00:17:35,169
He also follows up
with the next attack quickly.

224
00:17:42,217 --> 00:17:44,595
The best part is…

225
00:17:47,014 --> 00:17:49,641
this amazing power!

226
00:17:49,725 --> 00:17:52,478
This tiny body has stronger power than me.

227
00:17:52,561 --> 00:17:55,647
So he can cause a blow
with a small amount of cursed energy.

228
00:17:56,148 --> 00:18:00,569
So it's difficult to predict his actions
from the cursed energy flow!

229
00:18:00,652 --> 00:18:04,114
However, this delayed cursed energy…

230
00:18:04,198 --> 00:18:07,159
Only this…

231
00:18:08,494 --> 00:18:11,789
It's wrong!

232
00:18:11,872 --> 00:18:18,504
It's wrong!

233
00:18:24,301 --> 00:18:26,220
Was that Todo?

234
00:18:26,762 --> 00:18:28,097
I guess so.

235
00:18:28,180 --> 00:18:33,268
I vaguely understand
why you can't get rid of Yuji.

236
00:18:34,269 --> 00:18:37,564
So why did you separate from Noritoshi?

237
00:18:37,648 --> 00:18:40,692
Are you hiding your cursed techniques
from your own people?

238
00:18:45,322 --> 00:18:47,950
I'm sorry about Itadori.

239
00:18:48,450 --> 00:18:52,204
It may sound like an excuse,
but I'm not like the others.

240
00:18:52,287 --> 00:18:57,292
However, I don't intend
to let you guys win the Goodwill Event.

241
00:18:57,793 --> 00:18:58,919
RECOMMENDATION

242
00:18:59,002 --> 00:19:02,714
You know a Jujutsu Sorcerer's promotion
depends on recommendations, right?

243
00:19:03,298 --> 00:19:05,384
Even Jujutsu Sorcerers
with no direct contact

244
00:19:05,467 --> 00:19:08,053
will know about the Goodwill Event.

245
00:19:08,804 --> 00:19:10,973
Students who stand out
in the Goodwill Event

246
00:19:11,056 --> 00:19:14,726
have a higher chance for promotion
during the schooling period.

247
00:19:15,936 --> 00:19:20,065
By the way, you can't recommend
your own students.

248
00:19:20,566 --> 00:19:25,237
For example, Mr. Gojo
can't recommend Itadori to Grade 1.

249
00:19:25,904 --> 00:19:30,242
I want to be independent
as soon as possible and earn a living.

250
00:19:34,830 --> 00:19:35,831
Why?

251
00:19:38,750 --> 00:19:39,960
Because I'm poor.

252
00:19:40,043 --> 00:19:41,753
And I have two younger brothers!

253
00:19:41,837 --> 00:19:43,672
Are you okay?

254
00:19:43,755 --> 00:19:45,799
Are you getting along with Mai?

255
00:19:45,883 --> 00:19:47,426
Aren't you being too nice?

256
00:19:47,509 --> 00:19:48,385
What?

257
00:19:48,886 --> 00:19:50,220
I guess.

258
00:19:51,430 --> 00:19:53,599
I won't go easy on you.

259
00:19:54,933 --> 00:19:56,310
No problem.

260
00:19:56,393 --> 00:19:59,104
I'm not saying this
to make you show mercy.

261
00:20:01,690 --> 00:20:03,066
My friend.

262
00:20:03,150 --> 00:20:07,988
That delayed cursed energy
is your bad habit!

263
00:20:08,071 --> 00:20:09,615
You mean the Divergent Fist?

264
00:20:10,616 --> 00:20:12,993
What's with this guy?

265
00:20:14,453 --> 00:20:18,373
You can never beat me
so long as you're satisfied with this.

266
00:20:19,208 --> 00:20:25,380
We're no longer best friends
if you're satisfied with this level.

267
00:20:25,464 --> 00:20:27,299
